// The Bone Bridge (bible 8.1, [F 3.4]; saltmarrow-arc.md): Sable rows Wren under the whale's bones while the Bone
// Bridge commission is taken, and does not sing along. The whale's song is Runa's roll-call (3.4), heard here before
// Emberdown gives it words. She stands at the bridge's edge while the commission is taken and until she has rowed
// (FlagPresence, the recipe's NpcWhen); the quay keeps her otherwise.

title: BoneBridge_Sable
---
<<if has_flag("saltmarrow.bone_bridge.rowed")>>
    Sable: Rowed you once. The boat's not a ferry. #still #face:wary #line:0b5884c
    <<stop>>
<<endif>>
Sable: Thought you'd come this way. The reeds said so; they say everything twice. #line:0d7f7ca
Sable: Under the bridge the water's flat. That's where he is. Get in. I'll row; you listen. #line:0097578
<<sing whale>>
Sable: No. I don't sing it. Everyone on this coast knows the tune and nobody knows the words. #plant:3.4 #face:grave #line:0b50a76
-> It's a list. Those are names. #line:0d148ec
    <<voice surveyor saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Names, counts, prayers. Depends who's listening. A miner would say names. #plant:3.4 #line:0e820ba
-> You know the words. You're not saying them. #line:02f23fc
    <<voice warden saltmarrow>>
    Sable: I know eleven hundred and six words, and they're boats. Ask me those. #face:wary #line:0ffce9c
-> ... #line:05a3423
    <<voice drift saltmarrow>>
    Sable: Aye. That's the right answer under here. He likes the quiet ones. #face:bright #line:005af47
Sable: There. Other side. Bones over your head the whole way and you never looked up. Nobody does, the first time. #line:0ac6feb
<<flag saltmarrow.bone_bridge.rowed 1>>
===
